 #uuid "d0713573-1091-5dc9-a76b-4b2ca4946e18" :answer-field/key "field-13" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418983} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36aa71bb-abd4-5e7d-bf40-342563309bf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418813} {:answer/id #uuid "a3f53b19-2c77-56ea-9d4f-0f6324901acf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418872} {:answer/id #uuid "b5202bdc-3f5b-59bf-b24d-be7b9adda0f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5202bdc-3f5b-59bf-b24d-be7b9adda0f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418888} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6dee24c-3428-5bbe-a797-5223069d0102" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418984} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "851e3ac3-c97c-5623-8c07-ffb5b6529085" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418854} {:answer/id #uuid "f4487631-5b43-59ce-bfb1-0b0ef95f8f6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418933}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4487631-5b43-59ce-bfb1-0b0ef95f8f6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418933} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4f78005-0cf9-55e0-9cfd-7841d72569fa" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418985}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1bc13b0e-7f8a-5b76-a219-9d833008d899" :question/math-academy-id "q-183431" :question/problem "Use mathematical induction to prove that ${3}^{n}\\ge (n+1)^{2}$ for $n\\ge 2,n\\in N.$\n\nWe proceed using induction on $n.$\n\n**Base Case**: We first prove that our statement is true for the base case $n=\\,${{field-1}}.\n\nFor the left-hand side, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{field-2}}={{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is\n{{field-4}}\nthe right-hand side.\nThus, our statement is {{field-5}} for $n=2.$\n\n**Inductive Hypothesis**: We assume that for some $n=$ {{field-6}}, we have\n\n$$\n{{field-7}}\\ge {{field-8}}.\n$$\n\n**Inductive Step**: We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{field-9}}={{field-10}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand by the inductive hypothesis, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\cdot {3}^{k} & \\ge {{field-11}} \\\\  & ={{field-12}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & >{{field-13}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nas required.\n\nTherefore, by the principle of induction, ${3}^{n}\\ge (n+1)^{2}$ is true for all\n{{field-14}}." :question/worked-solution "A variant of the principle of induction states the following: Let ${n}_{0}$ be an integer. Suppose we have a sequence of mathematical statements $P({n}_{0}),P({n}_{0}+1),P({n}_{0}+2),…,$ where\n\n- $P({n}_{0})$ is true, and\n\n- $P(k)⇒P(k+1)$ for every integer $k\\ge {n}_{0}.$\n\nThen, $P(n)$ is true for every integer $n\\ge {n}_{0}.$\n\nIn this case, the general statement $P(n)$ we're required to prove is the following:\n\n$$\n{3}^{n}\\ge (n+1)^{2}\\,\\text{for}\\,n\\ge 2.\n$$\n\nWe start by proving the so-called base case, $P(2).$ To do this, we substitute $n=2$ into both the left-hand side and right-hand side and show that the left-hand side is greater than the right-hand side:\n\nWe proceed using induction on $n.$\n\n**Base Case**: We first prove our statement is true for the base case $n=2.$\nFor the left-hand side, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{2}=9,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for the right-hand side, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2+1)^{2}=9,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, our statement is true for $n=2.$\n\nNext, we state our inductive hypothesis. Here, we assume that the given statement is true for some $n=k\\ge 2.$ \n\n**Inductive Hypothesis**: We assume that for some $n=k\\ge 2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{3}^{k}\\ge (k+1)^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe must show that $P(k)⇒P(k+1).$ Let's start by writing down $P(k+1).$ This is the first part of the so-called **inductive step**.\n\n**Inductive Step**: We're required to prove that\n\n$$\n{3}^{k+1}\\ge (k+2)^{2}.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThe idea is to rewrite the left-hand side of $(∗)$ *using the inductive hypothesis* and apply algebraic techniques to show that this is greater than the right-hand side. We do this as follows:\n\nWe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{k+1} & ={3}^{k}\\cdot {3}^{1} \\\\  & =3\\cdot {3}^{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand by the inductive hypothesis, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\cdot \\,\\,\\,\\,{{{3}^{k}}_{⏟}}_{\\ge \\,(k+1)^{2}} & \\ge 3(k+1)^{2} \\\\  & =3{k}^{2}+6k+3 \\\\  & =(k+2)^{2}+{{2{k}^{2}+2k-1}_{⏟}}_{>0} \\\\  & >(k+2)^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nas required.\n\nSince we've shown that the left-hand side of $(∗)$ is greater than or equal to the right-hand side, our proof is complete. So, let's write down our conclusion. \n\nTherefore, by the principle of induction, ${3}^{n}\\ge (n+1)^{2}$ for all $n\\ge 2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092616 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092190 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b83c640f-c7fd-5adc-94b8-b129d357b140" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Polynomial Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99ebb4a8-9428-5176-87d5-0323e4e2ca13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089968} {:answer/id #uuid "083ceab8-7b48-5ad2-a20a-a3e419b8063e" :answer/type {:db/i